}^{2} & ={1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =1+3 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =4 \\\\ R & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-107553/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dba0779-e903-5281-bc41-01b78c31a98c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107553"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327669/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "74765624-2997-556c-bb1d-96da05bb7da0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327669/field-1/4a03be6ca5a931097242157323e96fac707848be6f9e14b789a4470740e06647" :answer/id #uuid "b22eb970-03fb-5ee4-b8e1-f0ace298ff5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "121" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327669/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1003564f-4545-5b97-90dc-4d5adaced41e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327669/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer-field/choices ["q-327669/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" "q-327669/field-1/4a03be6ca5a931097242157323e96fac707848be6f9e14b789a4470740e06647"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327669" :question/id #uuid "50f75dc0-69cb-5287-84d4-979b01969621" :question/math-academy-id "q-327669" :question/problem "Given that the expression $7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$\n\n$R=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=7 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=6\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={7}^{2}+(6\\sqrt{2})^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =49+72 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =121 \\\\ R & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-327669/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dba0779-e903-5281-bc41-01b78c31a98c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327669"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327678/field-1/c0d8d40f9c862082dbe940dc27a67b27277b8af7a60c9361f1a092b31e20a744" :answer/id #uuid "bf88c5a6-9ff2-57e0-a58b-d8095138c533" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327678/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed1c6879-8d2a-52e2-a9f8-f6b0da0ebbeb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327678/field-1/c0d8d40f9c862082dbe940dc27a67b27277b8af7a60c9361f1a092b31e20a744" :answer-field/choices ["q-327678/field-1/c0d8d40f9c862082dbe940dc27a67b27277b8af7a60c9361f1a092b31e20a744"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327678" :question/id #uuid "1804472b-fa65-568f-bf51-ed15b870bb4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-327678" :question/problem "Given that the expression $9\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$\n\n$R=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n9\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n9\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=9 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={9}^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =81+9 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =90 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{90} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-327678/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dba0779-e903-5281-bc41-01b78c31a98c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327678"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80134/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" :answer/id #uuid "0b464c4c-5424-5b68-90ee-8a3a1ea2aac9" :answe