e written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=3 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ ϕ & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80134/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80134"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327979/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "17d51fa9-e55e-56a6-b3c7-3bfdcb6468f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327979/field-1/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "34cd456b-03d7-5b40-b2d4-4bf35537c125" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327979/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c4a84f0-1887-5f8a-8f60-ebafa1362b37" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327979/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer-field/choices ["q-327979/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-327979/field-1/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327979" :question/id #uuid "4162ecbe-b322-51b0-80d6-aa2e8ed16fcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-327979" :question/problem "Given that the expression $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0,$ what is the **exact** value of $ϕ?$\n\n$ϕ=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡($ \n{{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-327979/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327979"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274585/field-1/ed43d5224151224cedff9572a0bc31a320bd7a8ebd2aa526ca5884904c9d6cb4" :answer/id #uuid "8f953393-db97-5831-b323-7470d8f8b027" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274585/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2910800d-3403-5c44-ab6a-1d19da820ae7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274585/field-1/ed43d5224151224cedff9572a0bc31a320bd7a8ebd2aa526ca5884904c9d6cb4" :answer-field/choices ["q-274585/field-1/ed43d5224151224cedff9572a0bc31a320bd7a8ebd2aa526ca5884904c9d6cb4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274585" :question/id #uuid "7d578acc-7046-58d2-ae73-9435d8a6fb2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-274585" :question/problem "Given that the expression $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the **exact** value of $ϕ?$\n\n$ϕ=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡($ \n{{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{9}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-274585/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80136/selection/3b28495977b1653d3b265084c301e2471a25911cfc996ab9fb4d1bd2f087ac51" :answer/id #uuid "cd174f26-5fb1-5c28-891e-44b1e55f59dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80136/selection/7309810f81f246b9935f0c7476dbf6c5de8cf4e653ca7c4040ccff721e7ccaff" :answer/id #uuid "88a1db87-659b-529e-bc5c-74574970ddc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80136/selection/9eeb04928e78de27a43522698093a84a4f743c9bffa5d13016a5d5e027b7f058" :answer/id #uuid "d9ce1e94-2fa2-5964-96e0-99175e831e90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80136/selection/fd43809a75a6874a90720f2e63a0e03c195dc672842ac92e44da4ef34609ef5a" :answer/id #uuid "f7a9f6a9-8147-5b11-b7bf-290651e0f5cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80136/selection/5454853a817db13094918bdbe0e10a99656ff85367ab90ccd985c0d49438056b" :answer/id #uuid "c078a503-fa99-5853-a262-b1e85aa61