{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{8}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =4 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80136/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80136"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107565/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" :answer/id #uuid "21967a74-a70c-5d80-9061-e2f8238e3b79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107565/selection/0ce4cdf24ea0065afc1ca1aa3662482333335a4ba13685e5f9035d4b2c16baef" :answer/id #uuid "ce34e396-33a4-584c-9f1d-8f7056a38a5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107565/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" :answer/id #uuid "ec117651-6ebe-569e-b39f-3266d56d5381" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107565/selection/78c3858d1a7b575a1a508fe78fa618d10c86698a24a8c9e8621b91963acfdf7d" :answer/id #uuid "623ea025-1e92-59f8-926d-0d25222e7e29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107565/selection/fb5de363a10a2104545417831042908dd07727135e2f3711a52dc6372478c77a" :answer/id #uuid "7a963b7b-2737-594d-9e91-6c643c1b46ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107565/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c858464a-8f09-513f-bda6-85d1356abf8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107565/selection/0ce4cdf24ea0065afc1ca1aa3662482333335a4ba13685e5f9035d4b2c16baef" :answer-field/choices ["q-107565/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" "q-107565/selection/0ce4cdf24ea0065afc1ca1aa3662482333335a4ba13685e5f9035d4b2c16baef" "q-107565/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" "q-107565/selection/78c3858d1a7b575a1a508fe78fa618d10c86698a24a8c9e8621b91963acfdf7d" "q-107565/selection/fb5de363a10a2104545417831042908dd07727135e2f3711a52dc6372478c77a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107565" :question/id #uuid "f3afc8de-0496-5d66-b501-f8daf7600278" :question/math-academy-id "q-107565" :question/problem "Given that the expression $\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107565/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107565"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11290/selection/d38c66fda4de23d784bf9b4ca60c3efb91e396fbcdf6ed05df7c7dd1bd6ceded" :answer/id #uuid "3bffc759-a98c-5e1c-afb4-124935b6cb31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.983)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11290/selection/b971f8dfcae3c44e0ebcda59ec6c74b247536e2cc9bd7bb72e34c0a98792d6b7" :answer/id #uuid "58bc3898-4677-5ce6-8dc4-1dbe681cde2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.983)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11290/selection/53a136342beed7e5e0887b0a4a7932cd47b295a04f50e1096727f8b474b0548f" :answer/id #uuid "fcd55a3b-d2f6-532f-a8a7-9e3d87cd177f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.983)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11290/selection/b7f3572b51beba5862e97ed20cf921c1cf5661c3703451116b488e206ff15512" :answer/id #uuid "54295dc2-6ea1-517e-a767-26ef7d899b91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.415)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11290/selection/c5ac7cd7c449d005fd18b7745276bcc6eeb563e3df78e62fa6cda19e9f606bf2" :answer/id #uuid "31db00b1-6e93-58eb-89e3-516c7fa18a6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+1.341)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11290/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c9ba608-5fa8-506a-9a4b-ae53a1df3160" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11290/selection/53a136342beed7e5e0887b0a4a7932cd47b295a04f50e1096727f8b474b0548f" :answer-field/choices ["q-11290/selection/d38c66fda4de23d784bf9b4ca60c3efb91e396fbcdf6ed05df7c7dd1bd6ceded" "q-11290/selection/b971f8dfcae3c44e0ebcda59ec6c74b247536e2cc9bd7bb72e34c0a98792d6b7" "q-11290/selection/53a136342beed7e5e0887b0a4a7932cd47b295a04f50e1096727f8b474b0548f" "q-11290/selection/b7f3572b51beba5862e97ed20cf921c1cf5661c3703451116b488e206ff15512" "q-11290/selection/c5ac7cd7c449d005fd18b7745276bcc6eeb563e3df78e62fa6cda19e9f606bf2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11290" :question/id #uuid "dc540d3e-160b-508c-ac71-1f1bf7873440" :question/math-academy-id "q-11290" :question/problem "$2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & =(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\ ϕ & ≈0.983\\,\\text{rad}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(ϕ)+{R}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡(ϕ) & ={3}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡(ϕ)+{cos}^{2}⁡(ϕ)) & =9+4 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =13 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)≈\\sqrt{13}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.983)\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11290/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11290"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107570/selection/e376072fe18c92a7ff166ab8e4a477d1abbe2b2aaf24411a85cbf90d01c8fcfe" :answer/id #uuid "9cf03b85-b86e-5971-811c-8e42af13f8bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107570/selection/3968119e3be67acfe540a9e3ddccc617aecbda9d13bad6f69969010c97783dc8" :answer/id #uuid "36ca2e08-c2e0-511e-bda0-599a38f224b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107570/selection/d115b80253f5c875b957868dfd7060643279f1a148437bc38a0f01950914ae5b" :answer/id #uuid "e1827cd8-b4b5-5ddf-9256-bc067ce409d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{60}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107570/selection/f7d75b99a499707bee258d9a8374ef416eb71e7a24baa5431df480952f74cafc" :answer/id #uuid "71055321-8af4-5fbd-8e12-a326c82c546d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{30}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107570/selection/663149b5a5e50fb679df105bad766405db265e889b3e9d760bd4a977becbff00" :answer/id #uuid "3a7ba58a-798a-5807-b249-708a5c5b9a73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{30}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107570/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a45f2153-4683-5fa9-9617-143881db98aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107570/selection/e376072fe18c92a7ff166ab8e4a477d1abbe2b2aaf24411a85cbf90d01c8fcfe" :answer-field/choices ["q-107570/selection/e376072fe18c92a7ff166ab8e4a477d1abbe2b2aaf24411a85cbf90d01c8fcfe" "q-107570/selection/3968119e3be67acfe540a9e3ddccc617aecbda9d13bad6f69969010c97783dc8" "q-107570/selection/d115b80253f5c875b957868dfd7060643279f1a148437bc38a0f01950914ae5b" "q-107570/selection/f7d75b99a499707bee258d9a8374ef416eb71e7a24baa5431df480952f74cafc" "q-107570/selection/663149b5a5e50fb679df105bad766405db265e889b3e9d760bd4a977becbff00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107570" :question/id #uuid "29f6ea73-9de7-55dd-ae3c-4a1047548a03" :question/math-academy-id "q-107570" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{5} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1 \\\\  & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(\\sqrt{5})^{2}+(\\sqrt{5})^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =5+5 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =10 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\sqrt{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107570/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107570"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107577/selection/6022d439fe92663896e1ca5bf6bb6f152c5e636a064121ad780f7e2201cafaca" :answer/id #uuid "ca59d549-212d-5afa-a3a0-be266414dd28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+1.107)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107577/selection/798345e7a441fee8d720e630811d43a654be71a51889172c016992b9d967043c" :answer/id #uuid "10598812-0f6a-5d50-bf5a-847740aef2d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+1.351)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107577/selection/6ee4e11494cc76cb427c7bcb5abfb957fb2e5e2b35fa43de900eb25c5d45f8d3" :answer/id #uuid "3415ec0b-63df-5359-ada7-30638d1b4f16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+0.464)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107577/selection/38b5abfb6c15161dbbac8075957a544fbce576b1f9d10ca958762c91445d48b0" :answer/id #uuid "959266a1-b43b-5ccf-85f5-33feb2ee6293" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+1.107)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107577/selection/a95cfcff3635eb0fa8804d6f3f207e33aaff00128bc162604cd984258bbc5cd9" :answer/id #uuid "b96f504f-5d44-5838-a29e-902c6f03b066" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+1.150)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107577/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8723bed-db8d-58c9-bc0f-1d4124803bc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107577/selection/6022d439fe92663896e1ca5bf6bb6f152c5e636a064121ad780f7e2201cafaca" :answer-field/choices ["q-107577/selection/6022d439fe92663896e1ca5bf6bb6f152c5e636a064121ad780f7e2201cafaca" "q-107577/selection/798345e7a441fee8d720e630811d43a654be71a51889172c016992b9d967043c" "q-107577/selection/6ee4e11494cc76cb427c7bcb5abfb957fb2e5e2b35fa43de900eb25c5d45f8d3" "q-107577/selection/38b5abfb6c15161dbbac8075957a544fbce576b1f9d10ca958762c91445d48b0" "q-107577/selection/a95cfcff3635eb0fa8804d6f3f207e33aaff00128bc162604cd984258bbc5cd9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107577" :question/id #uuid "db0aa66b-7e8e-5027-b840-3d5fc4d9828f" :question/math-academy-id "q-107577" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)≈$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{5} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =2 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2) \\\\  & =1.107\\,\\text{rad}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(\\sqrt{5})^{2}+(2\\sqrt{5})^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =5+4\\cdot 5 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =25 \\\\ R & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)≈5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+1.107)\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-107577/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107577"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80138/selection/0332f48092973728a9ab19a7d38d1fed8392bea3bd464b48824f5a638f7820c4" :answer/id #uuid "df969370-b77a-5be5-a0d2-e799792bf0bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80138/selection/d213ff681fe8bff2edef23f37d0d9ef15a8c725941d2a29ddbe827ba01d2af13" :answer/id #uuid "6901f3e0-5624-5f77-a3aa-87c4984f6297" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{30}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80138/selection/a72edc5c5258ac4c263b574bb301b714967482f738673028d27c7f8bc59b2828" :answer/id #uuid "9003f9cc-5c96-5514-a21b-f2d188f5ea67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80138/selection/1d7bd31ade8b8b8a57f2a07a29dc062b8c7446dbb4cd46c1716672c54324daf7" :answer/id #uuid "4f2f0117-d544-539b-b124-c48f8d1c1dcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80138/selection/eb041cff776875e7832060396e4933134accf33f77ea7d1f1571bb28d37870e1" :answer/id #uuid "408a0019-85f9-54c0-ad93-61d915471af9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{60}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80138/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "744e7dfb-4457-5ac4-a821-f53b644c029b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80138/selection/1d7bd31ade8b8b8a57f2a07a29dc062b8c7446dbb4cd46c1716672c54324daf7" :answer-field/choices ["q-80138/selection/0332f48092973728a9ab19a7d38d1fed8392bea3bd464b48824f5a638f7820c4" "q-80138/selection/d213ff681fe8bff2edef23f37d0d9ef15a8c725941d2a29ddbe827ba01d2af13" "q-80138/selection/a72edc5c5258ac4c263b574bb301b714967482f738673028d27c7f8bc59b2828" "q-80138/selection/1d7bd31ade8b8b8a57f2a07a29dc062b8c7446dbb4cd46c1716672c54324daf7" "q-80138/selection/eb041cff776875e7832060396e4933134accf33f77ea7d1f1571bb28d37870e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80138" :question/id #uuid "7349c862-48b2-5cc6-aa44-b59bdf12d6a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-80138" :question/problem "$4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{4}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) \\\\ ϕ & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={4}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =16+16 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =32 \\\\ R & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80138/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80138"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80144/selection/a3d55aeb3734fadbd5aa3e0cbd56dcedb2b7156f792c0076dd7e45bc2153626f" :answer/id #uuid "9a962bea-050d-5472-8938-5bbdea366289" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+1.101)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80144/selection/ec616e212db2f9c9ac526be96f435b785243437c732e9520f4acbc01370eba00" :answer/id #uuid "69729c8c-6055-570d-b3d4-e6bb127d198a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+1.710)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80144/selection/ff57c17f99c33bd5e84b7ff39cab10a2a2779f9a9760dbf967b42bf0b34c8c11" :answer/id #uuid "5ff6401a-80a6-550a-ae1b-f5073686ff42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+1.107)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80144/selection/f22ef92cd2b19612d6a0cd01de0352c945f5fef662245abe3df685a4fece15c2" :answer/id #uuid "aa166b74-294f-5416-a234-63522777fe9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+1.035)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80144/selection/beac0531bc9cc70f64e85532bc9e47051a0378515b3b8c7a87c809bc451aadc6" :answer/id #uuid "c975570d-e26c-50d5-b151-96a7f4be162c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+1.120)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80144/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b9e3e3e-1ec7-5b80-a593-77f23ba1d408" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80144/selection/ff57c17f99c33bd5e84b7ff39cab10a2a2779f9a9760dbf967b42bf0b34c8c11" :answer-field/choices ["q-80144/selection/a3d55aeb3734fadbd5aa3e0cbd56dcedb2b7156f792c0076dd7e45bc2153626f" "q-80144/selection/ec616e212db2f9c9ac526be96f435b785243437c732e9520f4acbc01370eba00" "q-80144/selection/ff57c17f99c33bd5e84b7ff39cab10a2a2779f9a9760dbf967b42bf0b34c8c11" "q-80144/selection/f22ef92cd2b19612d6a0cd01de0352c945f5fef662245abe3df685a4fece15c2" "q-80144/selection/beac0531bc9cc70f64e85532bc9e47051a0378515b3b8c7a87c809bc451aadc6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80144" :question/id #uuid "84950e34-628d-580f-b5fe-6a932ca0b240" :question/math-academy-id "q-80144" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & =(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=1 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =2 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2) \\\\ ϕ & ≈1.107\\,\\text{rad}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(ϕ)+{R}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡(ϕ) & ={2}^{2}+{1}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡(ϕ)+{cos}^{2}⁡(ϕ)) & =4+1 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =5 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)≈\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+1.107)\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80144/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80144"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274614/field-1/ccc5b7f3cfdb4c2dfc0e1f31be54559a1ab3adaf142e500fc1f1b7bc87e93b08" :answer/id #uuid "0657045b-0b3e-56fc-8062-ef4ab99cbe25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274614/field-1/438469ab2d71e1bb8b63f3164bacb1bbb54e29062b14dce6a666b63ac0081609" :answer/id #uuid "5e2dfc68-3038-51cc-ae0b-0fd760e9168e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274614/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1148039f-d63d-5289-8426-0bf26f7e02d4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274614/field-1/ccc5b7f3cfdb4c2dfc0e1f31be54559a1ab3adaf142e500fc1f1b7bc87e93b08" :answer-field/choices ["q-274614/field-1/ccc5b7f3cfdb4c2dfc0e1f31be54559a1ab3adaf142e500fc1f1b7bc87e93b08" "q-274614/field-1/438469ab2d71e1bb8b63f3164bacb1bbb54e29062b14dce6a666b63ac0081609"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274614" :question/id #uuid "8f4bdd81-7209-5e16-bfc5-a1fd0121d6ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-274614" :question/problem "Given that the expression $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-ϕ)$ with $0<ϕ<\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $R>0,$ what is the value of $ϕ?$\n\n$ϕ=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for cosine gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=1 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\ ϕ & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-274614/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12d8028-2520-5706-ba49-d67935036af6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274614"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65583/selection/7309810f81f246b9935f0c7476dbf6c5de8cf4e653ca7c4040ccff721e7ccaff" :answer/id #uuid "e0a13f3f-a856-5d39-9b1a-1ed8a5151b0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65583/selection/3a39027d6530a1dd904fd0cc078fc05421064e9482bf795d4962fbe927f847f8" :answer/id #uuid "47f8339f-00ac-51ff-996f-b705e179817c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65583/selection/739b5c6930b4c2b955ecca7e44f94c8ea216572c24283229109c401f42316193" :answer/id #uuid "f8e5e227-e80a-5231-a90b-1120051bba7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{8})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65583/selection/ec508878edfd1ac72232e580f5c036112ed6f0700297167c1140ceff806513c6" :answer/id #uuid "f13246d2-9194-57db-bffb-eda892501972" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65583/selection/b38d0d7bc461e2506975d9b6f933ec2d596cc1a748d25957ddea85e59e3147a7" :answer/id #uuid "b6b78dd8-b7d2-51da-9446-b85be5763818" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(8)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65583/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "49d04b26-e8e6-5c47-8533-c35a36b5a75e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-65583/selection/3a39027d6530a1dd904fd0cc078fc05421064e9482bf795d4962fbe927f847f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-65583/selection/7309810f81f246b9935f0c7476dbf6c5de8cf4e653ca7c4040ccff721e7ccaff" "q-65583/selection/3a39027d6530a1dd904fd0cc078fc05421064e9482bf795d4962fbe927f847f8" "q-65583/selection/739b5c6930b4c2b955ecca7e44f94c8ea216572c24283229109c401f42316193" "q-65583/selection/ec508878edfd1ac72232e580f5c036112ed6f0700297167c1140ceff806513c6" "q-65583/selection/b38d0d7bc461e2506975d9b6f933ec2d596cc1a748d25957ddea85e59e3147a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65583" :question/id #uuid "87b7b279-7595-56ef-b4fc-02a3f4fc0572" :question/math-academy-id "q-65583" :question/problem "Given that the expression $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-ϕ)$ with $0<ϕ<\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=8 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{8} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-65583/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12d8028-2520-5706-ba49-d67935036af6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107579/selection/8d714c1fd416e58da765395a7a57c526e1b97a45c41a59520f74d433a1e9ba87" :answer/id #uuid "d33c017c-0256-5ca6-9698-b9cd6cc16487" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107579/selection/1e940709a1b00fa910544fd0093551b452ea4b241ad5d9959525312e8a27fa19" :answer/id #uuid "0147be66-1ffa-5d03-8fc2-549e0a14ec7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107579/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" :answer/id #uuid "25236670-2fc6-5770-9bd5-2a0945d575e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107579/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "ebbb20a8-f88e-5089-a8b6-fa06637d95e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107579/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" :answer/id #uuid "8a7ca137-6015-53f7-b7a1-37ec317613a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107579/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d3fbc20-6bd4-55e8-837d-1abcc6494356" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107579/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" :answer-field/choices ["q-107579/selection/8d714c1fd416e58da765395a7a57c526e1b97a45c41a59520f74d433a1e9ba87" "q-107579/selection/1e940709a1b00fa910544fd0093551b452ea4b241ad5d9959525312e8a27fa19" "q-107579/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" "q-107579/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-107579/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107579" :question/id #uuid "2b668062-1203-5c59-8b5f-fabcb7916e31" :question/math-academy-id "q-107579" :question/problem "Given that the expression $2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with $0<ϕ<\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for cosine gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2\\sqrt{6} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\ ϕ & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107579/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12d8028-2520-5706-ba49-d67935036af6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107579"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274609/field-1/ccc5b7f3cfdb4c2dfc0e1f31be54559a1ab3adaf142e500fc1f1b7bc87e93b08" :answer/id #uuid "7b7b17ec-8aaa-5772-a0fc-5d2c5bee28d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274609/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "04c55e61-c577-55c9-90b3-2c61887c4e82" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274609/field-1/ccc5b7f3cfdb4c2dfc0e1f31be54559a1ab3adaf142e500fc1f1b7bc87e93b08" :answer-field/choices ["q-274609/field-1/ccc5b7f3cfdb4c2dfc0e1f31be54559a1ab3adaf142e500fc1f1b7bc87e93b08"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274609" :question/id #uuid "cec72bc3-9ce9-56a6-be97-f8888cf3eb33" :question/math-academy-id "q-274609" :question/problem "Given that the expression $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with $0<ϕ<\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $R>0,$ what is the value of $ϕ?$\n\n$ϕ=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for cosine gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=1 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\ ϕ & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-274609/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12d8028-2520-5706-ba49-d67935036af6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274609"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-30588/selection/4a2dfe599ef56af688d54531e6850f18c8824dda48d3967ac181adee78dee6a6" :answer/id #uuid "1b05f1ba-cbdb-5c22-ae61-26fd8698cfd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30588/selection/d76aba29f02c87309711dc1a1ec7d70367c9fde5693b26e4c76786b021502515" :answer/id #uuid "bd9b90bb-0591-5edb-8707-f322beaccd3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{2\\pi }{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30588/selection/337460c349176814e2ce8937047197db27acac1b00c854fa7caf55c6a3d4db09" :answer/id #uuid "055b7f47-2047-59ac-ab6b-db10bd1d99bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30588/selection/9e3a40fc6851a041fe13335d9b28df8fbe98e33eb61ebed0c6c25e07cbd9391f" :answer/id #uuid "7d80862d-ceed-5218-a10a-5fa7310fcca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30588/selection/d207c9cd052f181c942856aa2243e25b3a84d388ddc1e2a7715f0300a1554d53" :answer/id #uuid "7ae4900d-1807-5425-9844-93cf3e86d8cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{2\\pi }{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30588/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8fa1131c-da92-5cd8-8b0a-6ac1d605eea1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-30588/selection/4a2dfe599ef56af688d54531e6850f18c8824dda48d3967ac181adee78dee6a6" :answer-field/choices ["q-30588/selection/4a2dfe599ef56af688d54531e6850f18c8824dda48d3967ac181adee78dee6a6" "q-30588/selection/d76aba29f02c87309711dc1a1ec7d70367c9fde5693b26e4c76786b021502515" "q-30588/selection/337460c349176814e2ce8937047197db27acac1b00c854fa7caf55c6a3d4db09" "q-30588/selection/9e3a40fc6851a041fe13335d9b28df8fbe98e33eb61ebed0c6c25e07cbd9391f" "q-30588/selection/d207c9cd052f181c942856aa2243e25b3a84d388ddc1e2a7715f0300a1554d53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-30588" :question/id #uuid "6fd10193-69cb-5212-ac5c-9e4d5831b0e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-30588" :question/problem "$\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{2})}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\ ϕ & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {R}^{2} & =3 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-30588/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12d8028-2520-5706-ba49-d67935036af6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-30588"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
